<p begin="00:26:34.943" end="00:26:36.963" style="s2">[music]</p>
<p begin="00:26:46.078" end="00:26:48.098" style="s2">[music]</p>
<p begin="00:26:50.663" end="00:26:52.683" style="s2">[music]</p>
<p begin="00:27:06.383" end="00:27:08.403" style="s2">[music]</p>
<p begin="00:27:14.243" end="00:27:16.263" style="s2">[music]</p>
<p begin="00:27:27.998" end="00:27:30.018" style="s2">[music]</p>
<p begin="00:27:37.824" end="00:27:39.844" style="s2">[music]</p>
<p begin="00:27:46.994" end="00:27:49.014" style="s2">[applause]</p>
<p begin="00:27:53.409" end="00:27:57.109" style="s2">&gt;&gt; Thank you very much. That was John</p>
<p begin="00:27:54.909" end="00:27:59.409" style="s2">Philip Sousa&#39;s most famous march and our</p>
<p begin="00:27:57.109" end="00:28:01.709" style="s2">national march, The Stars and Stripes</p>
<p begin="00:27:59.409" end="00:28:03.409" style="s2">Forever. We&#39;ll move on now to a piece</p>
<p begin="00:28:01.709" end="00:28:05.509" style="s2">that was written for the Marine Band in</p>
<p begin="00:28:03.409" end="00:28:09.809" style="s2">honor of the United States Marine Corps.</p>
<p begin="00:28:05.509" end="00:28:09.809" style="s2">This is Robert Jager&#39;s Esprit de Corps.</p>
<p begin="00:28:40.704" end="00:28:42.724" style="s2">&gt;&gt; [music]</p>
